@startuml activity_path_weight_modes

skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12

title Path-Weight Modes — What Makes a Route "Best"?

start

:Select PathWeightMode;
note right
  CLI default: Solo
  Pathfinding API default: Distance
  Explicit options: --distance, --solo, --adaptive
  These choose the cost for one train;
  planner selection is a separate choice.
end note

if (Distance?) then (yes)
  :Dijkstra edge cost = distance (km);
  :Choose the route with the least total distance;
elseif (Solo?) then (yes)
  :Dijkstra edge cost = distance / speed limit;
  :Choose the fastest free-flow route;
else (Adaptive)
  :Base edge cost = distance / speed limit;
  :Add expected event delay\n(probability × duration);
  :When a live occupancy snapshot is supplied,\nadd a penalty if every line is occupied;
  :Choose the lowest-cost candidate route;
endif

:Run the simulation with the selected path;

if (Adaptive mode?) then (yes)
  :At eligible triggers, inspect a train\nbehind a slower leader;
  if (Leader continues beyond the next station?) then (yes)
    :Replay staying vs. a detour from that station;
    if (Detour saves more than 30 s?) then (yes)
      :Change the route at the station;
    else (no)
      :Keep the current route;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Keep the current route;
  endif
else (Distance or Solo)
  :No in-motion adaptive rerouting;
endif

note right
  Cooperative/CBS can separately reconsider routes of trains
  that have not departed after a rail event. This is planner
  behavior, not a PathWeightMode.
end note

stop

@enduml
